To compute the **convex hull** of a set of 2D points, the **Andrew's Monotone Chain Algorithm** is an efficient and elegant approach. This algorithm works by first sorting the points lexicographically (by x-coordinate, then y-coordinate), and then constructing the lower and upper hulls separately.

Here is the **complete and well-documented** implementation of the convex hull using Andrew's algorithm in **Rust**, with proper parsing of input and formatting of the output.

---

### ✅ **Rust Code: Convex Hull Using Andrew's Monotone Chain Algorithm**

```rust
use std::env;

// Helper function to compute the cross product of three points
fn cross(o: &(i32, i32), a: &(i32, i32), b: &(i32, i32)) -> i32 {
    (a.0 - o.0) * (b.1 - o.1) - (a.1 - o.1) * (b.0 - o.0)
}

fn main() {
    // Read command line arguments
    let args: Vec<String> = env::args().skip(1).collect();

    // Parse each point from the input
    let points: Vec<(i32, i32)> = args.iter()
        .map(|s| {
            let s = s.trim();
            let s = &s[1..s.len()-1]; // Remove parentheses
            let parts: Vec<&str> = s.split(',').collect();
            let x = parts[0].parse().unwrap();
            let y = parts[1].parse().unwrap();
            (x, y)
        })
        .collect();

    // Sort the points lexicographically
    let mut sorted = points.clone();
    sorted.sort_by(|a, b| {
        if a.0 != b.0 {
            a.0.cmp(&b.0)
        } else {
            a.1.cmp(&b.1)
        }
    });

    // Build the lower and upper hulls
    let mut lower = Vec::new();
    for &point in &sorted {
        while lower.len() >= 2 {
            let last = lower.last().unwrap();
            let second_last = lower[lower.len() - 2];
            if cross(&second_last, last, &point) <= 0 {
                lower.pop();
            } else {
                break;
            }
        }
        lower.push(point);
    }

    let mut upper = Vec::new();
    for &point in sorted.iter().rev() {
        while upper.len() >= 2 {
            let last = upper.last().unwrap();
            let second_last = upper[upper.len() - 2];
            if cross(&second_last, last, &point) <= 0 {
                upper.pop();
            } else {
                break;
            }
        }
        upper.push(point);
    }

    // Combine the lower and upper hulls, removing the duplicate point
    let mut hull = lower;
    hull.extend(upper.iter().rev().skip(1)); // Skip the first point of upper (already in lower)
    hull.pop(); // Remove the last duplicate point (the same as the first point in lower)

    // Format the output as a comma-separated list of points
    let output = hull.iter()
        .map(|&(x, y)| format!("({},{})", x, y))
        .collect::<Vec<String>>()
        .join(",");

    println!("{}", output);
}
